  "readmeFile": "README.NuGet.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.13.0. New: gift certificates and credit notes can be read (client.Sales.GiftCertificate and client.Sales.CreditNote, with settings and exact counts), and a sales invoice can be paid with gift certificates, give change as cash, a credit note, or forfeited, and sell gift certificates (Sales.Invoice.CreateWithGiftCertificatesAsync, GiftCertificateInvoiceOptions.Sell). The invoice must be posted and needs a Reference of 1 to 12 characters; redeeming needs every line priced explicitly with tax (no discount, no OriginalPrices), computes the total from those prices instead of a DK Plus price calculation, and throws when DK creates the invoice with another total; you supply the payment ids, which are checked against the dkERP payment modes (table SORUPM, not the payment-type endpoint, which can lag); nothing is retried or rolled back, and a pending step throws DkPlusGiftCertificateInvoiceException. MarkUsedAsync, ActivateAsync, and GiftCertificate.CreateAsync complete a pending step, and Sales.Invoice.FindByReferenceAsync checks an Unknown outcome. Verified live on a test company (2026-11-11): selling gift certificates, redeeming them with cash change, forfeit, and a credit-note change, marking certificates used, activating a change credit note, and recovery (mark used, create, and activate are idempotent on the same invoice and refused, with no write, on another); the invoices were fully settled and DK's created total equalled the computed one. Not verified live: automatic numbering and required barcodes (the test company has both off), the reference lookup after a failed create, and the posted-heads fallback read; try these on a test company first. Improvements: Table.GetRecordsAsync with a key filter and no maximum reads every matching row (the TableReadIncomplete warning is gone), and an unlimited table read refuses a full batch that is out of RECORDMODIFIED order. Fixes: an unset date (0001-01-01 or 1899-12-30) reads as null instead of a real date, in JSON responses and in table rows; table updates send the key column names in the path and the key values in the body, which DK Plus requires (verified live on a test company, 2026-11-11: exactly one row changed). Breaking: IDkPlusSalesResource and IDkPlusSalesInvoiceResource gain members (default members on .NET 10, abstract on netstandard2.0, so an own implementation must add them there), and table update takes the record through key field=value pairs instead of a positional key.",
